Upstream attribution — eli5
===========================

This package is a port of the `eli5` plugin for Claude Code.

Source:   https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-community
Path:     eli5/
Author:   Thariq Shihipar

The upstream plugin declares its own license in `eli5/.claude-plugin/plugin.json`:

    "author": { "name": "Thariq Shihipar" },
    "license": "MIT",

The upstream repository ships no MIT license text inside the `eli5/` directory,
so the standard MIT text is reproduced below under the declared author's name.

The repository itself is distributed by Anthropic under the Apache License 2.0
(see its root `LICENSE`), which likewise permits modification and
redistribution with attribution. Both notices are preserved here.

What was ported: the idea and the instructional intent of the skill — explain a
topic to someone who knows nothing about it, using a picture-heavy HTML page
with very few words. Everything else in this package (the extension, the
publishing tool, the cross-platform opener, the configuration, the tests, and
the rewritten SKILL.md) is original work by johnkai-kai, licensed under the
separate `LICENSE` file.


